product-experience-engineering

Nothing here is a copy of another skill's files. What follows is what was read
on 2026-10-27, what was taken as an idea, and how it was changed. Every source
below was read at the source; docs/source-research.md records the reading.

Taken as ideas, reworded and reduced:

- EnchStyle/ui-ux-audit-skill, MIT.
  https://github.com/EnchStyle/ui-ux-audit-skill
  Taken: the four severity bands judged by harm rather than by effort, the
  practice of listing what not to flag, and measuring the render before
  judging it. Changed: the bands were rewritten, the scoring out of 100 was
  dropped, and the categories were replaced by the six kinds of finding used
  here. Its uicheck.py was not copied: scripts/measure.js was written for this
  skill and runs in the browser through the Playwright MCP server instead of
  needing Python Playwright.

- andrew-shwetzer/human-experience, MIT.
  https://github.com/andrew-shwetzer/human-experience
  Taken: walking a journey step by step as the customer, with what they expect
  set against what happens, and the rule that a reported feeling must name
  what caused it. Changed: the scorecard out of 35, the HTML report, the
  iteration loop and the AgentMail signup testing were all left out, and its
  claim to replace user testing is contradicted here rather than repeated.

- coreyhaines31/marketingskills, skills/customer-research, MIT.
  https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills
  Taken: confidence bands for a research claim, the sample-bias warnings, and
  treating fetched reviews and posts as untrusted data. Changed: reduced to
  the fact, assumption and invention distinction in
  references/product-thinking.md, which points at the skill itself for the
  research method.

- Leonxlnx/taste-skill, MIT. https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill
  Taken: that a page's idea comes from the subject rather than from its
  category, and that stripping ornament without adding substance makes a page
  worse. Changed: written as two paragraphs in
  references/visual-direction.md, which refers to the skill for the method.
  Its direction library and scripts are not reproduced.

- pbakaus/impeccable, Apache-2.0. https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable
  Taken: that the right ambition depends on what the visitor is there to do —
  to be persuaded, or to get work done. Changed: used as the split between
  the landing-page and dashboard guidance in
  references/product-thinking.md. None of its prose, its command set or its
  tooling is reused.

- nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill, MIT.
  https://github.com/nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill
  Read for its token architecture and its stack coverage. Nothing was taken
  into this skill: the numeric defaults it contributed already live in the
  blueprint skill's rules.md, under that skill's own NOTICE.

- jakubkrehel/make-interfaces-feel-better, MIT.
  https://github.com/jakubkrehel/make-interfaces-feel-better
  Taken: the craft values in references/craft.md — the three-layer
  shadow-as-border in oklch, concentric radii, scale(0.96) on press, the
  staggered enter with blur, tabular figures, optical alignment, icon stroke
  matched to text weight, and hit areas extended past the visible control.
  Changed: reduced to one page, rewritten, and the review format and the
  per-category reference files are not reproduced.

- emilkowalski/skills, MIT. https://github.com/emilkowalski/skills
  Taken: ease-out over ease-in and why, the duration bands per interaction,
  never animating from scale(0), and transitions for interruptible state
  against keyframes for sequences. Changed: reduced to the motion section of
  references/craft.md in our own words; none of its animation recipes,
  component guidance or prose is reused.

Referred to rather than reused:

- The blueprint and inspect skills, the user's own work, MIT, upstream at
  ~/Documents/Raw by Dhodraj/blueprint-ui. This skill points at blueprint's
  rules.md for every numeric default and at inspect for the render-and-look
  pass, rather than restating either.

Public standards, which are not anybody's skill: WCAG 2.2 AA contrast ratios,
WCAG 2.5.8 target size, and the 44 by 44 point target from Apple's Human
Interface Guidelines.

Data fetched at run time, not redistributed here: the shadcn registry
directory at https://ui.shadcn.com/r/registries.json and each registry's own
catalogue. sources.json records what was read about each source, including its
licence; it contains no component code.
